                    briefing_text_r2:       `The core decision, within the <strong>฿18M</strong> budget. Choose an <em>ordering policy</em> (independent reorder-point, smaller/more-frequent orders, base-stock with smoothing, or coordinated replenishment), an <em>information-sharing level</em> (none, share POS demand, a shared forecast, or VMI/CPFR), and a <em>promotion policy</em> (deep periodic discounts, scheduled capacity-aware promos, or everyday-low-price). Each lever consumes budget and changes variance, cost and service. Smoothing your ordering rule while every tier still forecasts off distorted orders only dampens the wave — it does not remove the distortion that creates it.`,
