                    coach_default:          `Decision logged.`,
                    coach_r1_sharp:         `<strong>Sharp diagnosis.</strong> The amplification is cumulative and upstream — each tier forecasts off the distorted orders below it, so ±6% true demand becomes ±48% at the factory. Demand-signal processing is the dominant cause, and it is exactly what information-sharing attacks. You read it right before designing anything.`,
                    coach_r1_upstream:      `<strong>Right where it grows.</strong> The variance amplification ratio climbs at every tier going up the chain — wholesaler, DC, factory. Now make sure you name <em>why</em>: each tier is forecasting off orders, not retail demand.`,
                    coach_r1_factory:       `<strong>The factory feels the pain, but it is not the source.</strong> Reschedule the plant all you like — the ±48% swing is manufactured by four tiers each reacting to the one below. This is a chain coordination problem, not a production-scheduling one.`,
